Microsoft Events Guide - Privacy and Usage Analytics

Data Collection. The software may collect information about you and your use
of the software and send it to Microsoft. Microsoft may use this information
to provide services and improve our products and services. You may turn off
the telemetry as described in the repository. There are also some features
in the software that may enable you and Microsoft to collect data from users
of your applications. If you use these features, you must comply with
applicable law, including providing appropriate notices to users of your
applications together with a copy of Microsoft's privacy statement. Our
privacy statement is located at https://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/?LinkID=824704.
You can learn more about data collection and use in the help documentation
and our privacy statement. Your use of the software operates as your consent
to these practices.

The hosted app collects usage telemetry automatically, without a permission
prompt or cookie banner. Default local and PR builds do not collect application
telemetry. Run a local version to use the app without application analytics.

Usage records are restricted to event/catalog/session identities,
explicit action type/source/counts, ordered known-session composition,
schema/build/environment, and random action-scoped identifiers. They do not
include personal notes, custom titles/summaries, share tokens, URLs/referrers,
raw search text, account/email identities, or persistent visitor identities.
The SDK writes no tracking cookies or storage. Local event draft and agenda
storage is separate from application analytics.

To produce a telemetry-disabled version, set HUGO_TELEMETRY_ENABLED=false
when running the documented npm build/dev commands. This excludes the
analytics SDK and ingestion configuration from that build.

Usage retention is 730 days in the dedicated Azure AppEvents table.
The approved workspace ingestion transformation removes service-derived
browser, OS, device/location and visitor/session/operation identifiers before
new records are stored. It does not retroactively alter earlier smoke-test
records. Normal network infrastructure still processes request metadata.
Production collection requires valid deployment configuration. Verify stored
post-transformation rows.

Share links contain their snapshots and notes in the query string. Do not
include private information. Encoding is not encryption. A requested URL
may appear in hosting/access logs regardless of application analytics.
Disabling application analytics does not disable the hosting provider's logs.
